    <h1>Privacy Policy for Cozy Capsule</h1>
    <p class="meta"><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 16, 2026</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Cozy Capsule</strong>, developed by <strong>Ayoub Nmr</strong>, handles information when you use the application.</p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>The current version of Cozy Capsule does <strong>not collect, transmit, or store personal information on external servers</strong>.</p>
    <p>The app does not require an account and does not collect information such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name</li><li>Email address</li><li>Phone number</li><li>Precise or approximate location</li>
      <li>Contacts</li><li>Photos or files</li><li>Camera or microphone data</li>
      <li>Advertising identifiers</li><li>Payment information</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Local Game Data</h2>
    <p>Cozy Capsule stores limited gameplay information locally on your device so that your progress can be restored between sessions.</p>
    <p>This may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Collected items</li><li>Collection progress</li><li>Duplicate-item shards</li><li>Game preferences and settings</li></ul>
    <p>This information remains on your device and is not transmitted to us or to any external server.</p>

    <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
    <p>The current version of Cozy Capsule does <strong>not</strong> contain advertising SDKs and does not display advertisements.</p>
    <p>If advertising is introduced in a future version, this Privacy Policy will be updated before that version is released.</p>

    <h2>4. Analytics</h2>
    <p>The current version of Cozy Capsule does <strong>not</strong> use third-party analytics services.</p>
    <p>We do not currently collect gameplay analytics, device analytics, crash analytics, or behavioral tracking data through the app.</p>

    <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>The current version of Cozy Capsule does not send user data to third-party services for advertising, analytics, profiling, or marketing purposes.</p>
    <p>Google Play may independently process information related to downloading, installing, or distributing the application according to Google's own policies. Such processing is controlled by Google and is not performed by Cozy Capsule.</p>

    <h2>6. Permissions</h2>
    <p>Cozy Capsule does not request access to sensitive device permissions such as:</p>
    <ul><li>Location</li><li>Camera</li><li>Microphone</li><li>Contacts</li><li>Storage</li><li>Phone or call information</li></ul>

    <h2>7. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
    <p>Gameplay progress and settings are stored locally on your device.</p>
    <p>Local data generally remains available until you:</p>
    <ul><li>Clear the application's storage or data through Android settings; or</li><li>Uninstall Cozy Capsule.</li></ul>
    <p>Because Cozy Capsule does not currently provide user accounts or store personal gameplay data on our servers, there is no server-side account or personal gameplay record to delete.</p>

    <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
    <p>Cozy Capsule is designed to minimize data collection. The current version does not transmit personal or gameplay information to our servers.</p>
    <p>Locally stored application data is handled using the storage mechanisms provided by the Android operating system.</p>

    <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>Cozy Capsule does not knowingly collect personal information from children or other users.</p>
    <p>The current version does not provide account registration, social features, user-generated content, targeted advertising, or mechanisms for submitting personal information through the app.</p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated when Cozy Capsule changes its features or data-handling practices.</p>
    <p>For example, if advertising, analytics, online services, or other functionality that processes user data is introduced, this Privacy Policy will be revised accordingly.</p>
    <p>Any updated policy will show a revised "Last updated" date.</p>

